- @intro_1: And another day begins anew.

@intro_1
subtitle: Time to wake up!
new-page: true
go-to: option_intro

= An early morning

You wake up rather early in the morning as the sun is yet to be visible above the horizon.

You feel pleasantly surprised. It has been quite a while since you've managed to wake up this early, after all.

Taking a glance at the clock, you notice that there is still quite some time left before you have to go to the Royal Palace. As you prepare for the day, your mind begins wandering about...

@option_intro

- @myself: Yourself.
- @job: Your assigned tasks.
- @darlyne: The princess herself.
- @intro_news

@myself
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: intro_myself_seen = 1
go-to: option_intro

You are Levon, a youthful genius who was recently assigned to the prestigious post of Princess Darlyne's assistant.

You scored one of the highest final exam scores for both *Natural Alchemy* and *Law* in Nocturnia's history, and you hold a very high pride in becoming one of the few to achieve them.

@job
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: intro_job_seen = 1
go-to: option_intro

Your job nowadays is to help Princess Darlyne across various things, though it would mostly either revolve around her chemical research or... really, anything that piqued her interests.

As tiring as it might be sometimes, you can't help but be drawn into this job a little more with each passing day.

@darlyne
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: intro_darlyne_seen = 1
go-to: option_intro

Princess Darlyne Nightbloom is the sole daughter of the current King and Queen of Nocturnia. 

In public, she is a very quiet lady, rarely conversing more than a few minutes before drawing herself back into solitude. However, when she is truly comfortable or immersed in something (as she often did with her research), her energy is truly a sight to behold.

Nowadays, she is occupied with her deep fascination with love potions (or, in her own words, *"the mystical powers that unite hearts"*), and she has even got to be known as *Doctor of Love*. Though you are personally still unconvinced whether it is something worth pursuing, you don't mind helping her along the way as you should anyway.

Even after interacting so many times, she remains in your eyes as nothing short of an enigmatic prodigy.

@intro_news
title: And then...
view-if: intro_myself_seen and intro_job_seen and intro_darlyne_seen

Before you realize it, the sun is already well above the horizon, and the sky has already turned a rather bright blue.

You quickly finish up your preparation before heading towards the door. Everything is nicely put into the bag, and you are now ready to go.

- @head_out: It's time to head out.

@head_out
new-page: true

- @newspaper_1: The morning newspaper has arrived!

@newspaper_1
subtitle: You wonder what the headline has in store for the day.
new-page: true

The morning newspaper arrives in front of the door right as you are about to head out. Curious, you decide to pick it up to read what the headline said.

- @headline: And the headline reads...

@headline
audio: music/dadar_intro.mp3 loop

= REVEALED: THE CRIMES OF NOCTURNIA’S PRINCESS!

- @what: ...What?

@what

"Crimes of... the princess?"

Your eyes remain glued to the headline written in large, bold letters on the top of the newspaper. There is only one Princess of Nocturnia, after all. What has she done to warrant such an astounding, accusatory headline?

You decide to continue reading through the article on the next page.

- @accuse: ...Infidelity?

@accuse

"...Infidelity?" You whisper under your breath, eyes now open wide.

The article written on the newspaper accuses Princess Darlyne of being complicit in various acts of infidelity across Nocturnia and beyond. Even worse, the article included an interview with a villager who claimed to be a victim due to her vaguely-described "acts of complicity".

Gears begin turning inside your head. *Of course*, you think, *how could someone like Princess Darlyne be accused of something so vile?*

Granted, rumours about the Royal Family are not so rare amongst the common populace. Several underground newspapers have even gotten notoriously popular by publishing those kind of things. However, nothing that you've read or heard before could compare to the one you read just now.

- @posthink: Perhaps this is nothing but made-up rumours?

@posthink
on-arrival: brought_up = 0

You try to keep your thoughts positive, hoping that this would be nothing but a typical sensasionalist hearsay on a slow news day.

The sun is already shining brightly in the sky. You decide to fold the newspaper into the bag and hurry towards the Royal Palace. 

Those rumours can wait until the next break, after all... right?

- @first_meet_1

@first_meet_1
